- the PR homepage loads the same scripts and markup as `master`;
- the failing runner was about 40% slower on Lighthouse's CPU benchmark;
- `master` itself has swung from 0 to 1,125 ms on this test with unchanged code;
- alternating builds on one machine showed no regression.

That evidence is written up in the PR's report, `docs/launch-ready/PHASE-5-WEB-UX.md`. CI for draft PR [TheFridey/ScaleSmiths#161](https://github.com/TheFridey/ScaleSmiths/pull/161) is still running, and Auto-fix isn't on for it yet.
